    "overall_risk_rating": "HIGH",
    "narrative": "com.ocv.a834 is a community/church mobile app built on the OCV (Online Church Vision) platform. It embeds an unusually wide set of SDKs and declares a large number of sensitive permissions relative to its apparent purpose. The tracker stack includes Firebase Analytics + FCM (Google), Facebook SDK, Google AdMob (with Advertising ID collection), AWS Amplify + Amazon Pinpoint (a second independent analytics pipeline), BugSnag (crash and performance), and Google Maps/Location. The two most significant concerns are: (1) The simultaneous collection of precise GPS location (ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION) combined with AdMob Advertising ID collection â€” together these enable precise location-based ad profiling; and (2) The declaration of READ_SMS, READ_CALL_LOG, READ_CONTACTS, RECORD_AUDIO, and PROCESS_OUTGOING_CALLS permissions, which are highly sensitive and difficult to justify for a church community app. A Google YouTube API key is hardcoded in the DEX bytecode and is trivially extractable, creating a quota-abuse risk. No data broker SDKs (Kochava, X-Mode/Outlogic) were detected."
  },
